---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CERT_SHA256 } from '../i18n';
import Changelog from '../components/Changelog.astro';
---
<Page lang="en" page="changelog" title="Changelog – CastBay" description="What's new in each version of CastBay.">
<main class="wrap doc">
    <h1>Changelog</h1>
    <p class="date" set:html={`What changed in each version. Download the latest from <a href="https://github.com/weenas/castbay/releases/latest/download/CastBay.apk">CastBay.apk</a>, or any version from the <a href="https://github.com/weenas/castbay/releases">releases page</a>. Follow new versions with <a href="/changelog.xml">RSS</a>.`}></p>
    <details class="verify">
      <summary>Verify your download</summary>
      <p>Each version below lists its APK's SHA-256. Compare it with the file you downloaded: <code>shasum -a 256 CastBay-1.0.79.apk</code> on a Mac or Linux, <code>certutil -hashfile CastBay-1.0.79.apk SHA256</code> on Windows. (<code>CastBay.apk</code>, the latest version, is the same file as its numbered one.)</p>
      <p>Every release is signed with the same certificate (CN=CastBay, O=weenas), whose SHA-256 fingerprint is <code>{CERT_SHA256}</code>. <code>apksigner verify --print-certs</code>, from the Android SDK, shows it. Android also refuses to update CastBay with an APK signed by any other.</p>
    </details>
    <Changelog lang="en" />
</main>
</Page>
